# .cleanignore — what does NOT ship to the production repo (Dhyan-rao-10/Pratham-OPD).
#
# Gitignore syntax, matched against paths RELATIVE TO THIS FILE (opd-preconsult/),
# which are also the paths in the production repo (it has no opd-preconsult/ prefix).
#
# Used by scripts/sync-clean.py. Two things to understand:
#
#  1. The sync reads files from git (HEAD), never from your working tree. Untracked
#     files therefore CANNOT ship — .env, node_modules/, eval/, .next/ and friends are
#     already invisible and need no rule here. Rules below are for files that ARE
#     committed but must not be published.
#
#  2. Excluding a path also PROTECTS it in the production repo: the sync will not copy
#     it, and will not delete it if it already exists there. That is how the two seed
#     migrations below keep their production-specific contents.
#
# Do NOT add patterns matching "claude" or "anthropic" generally — the product legitimately
# calls the Anthropic API (llm_client.py, requirements.txt). Only CLAUDE.md is the tell,
# and the sync separately asserts that no shipped file even mentions it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI-assisted-development artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal process / mentor-facing working docs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Names collaborators and internal rules; not for the shared repo.
docs/changes-for-samvith.md
docs/mentor-questions.md
docs/bhasini-access-request.md
# Candid list of open vulnerabilities incl. an unfixed High. Real value for mentors, but
# publish it deliberately after a rewrite — not silently via a mirror.
docs/SECURITY_GAP_ANALYSIS.md
# Internal pilot tracking.
PILOT-CHECKLIST.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prototypes / experiments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never containerised (see .dockerignore), each carries its own .env, and none is
# imported by the app.
bhashini-lab/
ocr-lab/
stt-lab/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo seed data — THE ONLY DELIBERATE test/prod difference. Read before touching.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Here these seed 3 demo doctors (PIN 1234) + CARD/GEN so the app is testable.
# In production they seed a clean slate, so a fresh hospital deployment does NOT come up
# with demo logins. Both files are already applied in every existing database
# (schema_migrations is keyed on filename, so they never re-run) — they are frozen
# history, and excluding them is what keeps each side correct.
#
# Do NOT "fix" this divergence by removing these lines: that ships PIN-1234 doctors to
# every fresh hospital deployment. Every OTHER migration is byte-identical across repos.
db/migrations/005_doctors.sql
db/migrations/006_departments.sql

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The sync tooling itself
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is how the production repo is BUILT. Production does not build anything, and
# these files necessarily discuss CLAUDE.md/exclusions — which the sync's own assertion
# would (correctly) refuse to ship.
.cleanignore
scripts/sync-clean.py
SYNC.md
